 "conclusions": [
  "The op is callable on A5 with attention_mode=2 and non-null query_rope/key_rope; no package, CANN version, workspace, allocator or container restart is missing.",
  "Decode at V4 shape (128 q heads, 1 KV head, qk 512+64, v 512, top-k 2048) is flat at 0.0806-0.0821 ms for batch 1-4 and KV 32k/64k/128k: top-k and fixed dispatch dominate, not KV length.",
  "Scaling: time grows with top-k (0.056 ms at 256 -> 0.083 at 2048 -> 0.186 at 8192) while q heads (32/64/128) and batch (1/2/4/8) are flat; per-batch KV is loaded once for all 128 query heads.",
  "Chunked prefill q=1024 per request: batch 1 is 2.842/2.876/2.947 ms and batch 4 is 11.446/11.726/11.883 ms at KV 32k/64k/128k; time is linear in batch and each B=4 row equals the corresponding B=1 call exactly (rel 0.0)."
 ],
 "limitations": [
  "Synthetic tensors and random sorted top-k indices; no real V4 weights or paged KV content.",
  "Single die, single process, eager mode; ACL-graph replay would remove the ~30-50 us dispatch floor.",
  "PA_BSND rows use block_size 128; top-k 2048 all-valid (no -1 padding exercised).",
  "Prefill rows are chunked-prefill positions kv-q..kv-1 with causal-valid top-k, not a full V4 prompt prefill; batch 4 is four independent 1024-token requests.",
  "softmax_max/softmax_sum are empty [0] when return_softmax_lse=False."
 ],
